# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Pagsasaayos {#setup}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section imports the tools and defines the shell-model helpers the workflow needs, in the order\n"
"the workflow uses them. The physics behind each one is derived in the [Appendix](#appendix); the\n"
"comments describe each function's role in the workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini-import ng seksyong ito ang mga kasangkapan at dine-define ang mga shell-model helper na kailangan ng workflow, sa ayos na\n"
"ginagamit ito ng workflow. Ang physics sa likod ng bawat isa ay hinango sa [Appendix](#appendix); inilalarawan ng mga\n"
"comment ang papel ng bawat function sa workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two interaction files are unpacked first. Both are published parameter sets, embedded here so the\n"
"notebook is self-contained: `usda.snt` is the USDA $sd$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[2\\]](#references) and\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` is the GXPF1 $pf$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalawang interaction file ang unang binubuksan (unpack). Parehong mga nailathalang parameter set, na naka-embed dito upang ang\n"
"notebook ay self-contained: ang `usda.snt` ay ang USDA $sd$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[2\\]](#references) at\n"
"ang `gxpf1.snt` ay ang GXPF1 $pf$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The model space and the qubit register {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"
msgstr "Ang model space at ang qubit register {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An `.snt` file holds the model space, the single-particle energies, and the $J$-coupled two-body\n"
"matrix elements. For the mass-dependent interactions used here, the third and fourth fields of the two-body\n"
"header specify the reference mass\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ at which the interaction was fitted and the exponent of its mass dependence. Both\n"
"files carry the exponent $-0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for USDA and $42$ for GXPF1, so the\n"
"tabulated matrix elements must be rescaled by $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ for the nucleus being\n"
"computed [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Single-particle energies are not rescaled. Skipping\n"
"this step changes the correlation energy by a few percent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hawak ng isang `.snt` file ang model space, ang single-particle energies, at ang $J$-coupled two-body\n"
"matrix elements. Para sa mga mass-dependent na interaction na ginamit dito, ang ikatlo at ikaapat na field ng two-body\n"
"header ay tumutukoy sa reference mass\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ kung saan na-fit ang interaction at ang exponent ng mass dependence nito. Parehong\n"
"file ay may exponent na $-0.3$, kasama ang $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ para sa USDA at $42$ para sa GXPF1, kaya\n"
"dapat i-rescale ang mga naka-tabulang matrix element sa pamamagitan ng $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ para sa nucleus na\n"
"kinukwenta [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Hindi nire-rescale ang single-particle energies. Ang pagligtaan\n"
"sa hakbang na ito ay nagbabago sa correlation energy ng ilang porsyento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The energies that follow are *valence* energies, measured from the inert core; they are not experimental\n"
"separation energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga energy na sumusunod ay mga *valence* na energy, na sinusukat mula sa inert core; hindi ito mga eksperimental\n"
"separation energy.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clebsch-Gordan recoupling {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"
msgstr "Clebsch-Gordan recoupling {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Equation (2) requires Clebsch-Gordan coefficients for half-integer angular momenta. Every argument is\n"
"passed as *twice* its physical value, so $j = 5/2$ enters as `5` and the arithmetic stays exact.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nangangailangan ang Equation (2) ng mga Clebsch-Gordan coefficient para sa half-integer na angular momenta. Ang bawat argument ay\n"
"ipinapasa bilang *dalawang beses* ang pisikal na halaga nito, kaya ang $j = 5/2$ ay pumapasok bilang `5` at nananatiling eksakto ang arithmetic.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` handles lookups of the interaction matrix elements. An `.snt` file stores each\n"
"matrix element once, so a lookup might need the antisymmetrized pair-exchange phase $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ on either\n"
"side, and the bra and ket might be stored in either order.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hinahawakan ng `Interaction.v_ms` ang mga lookup ng interaction matrix element. Iniimbak ng isang `.snt` file ang bawat\n"
"matrix element nang isang beses lamang, kaya maaaring kailanganin ng lookup ang antisymmetrized pair-exchange phase na $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ sa alinmang\n"
"panig, at maaaring naka-imbak ang bra at ket sa alinmang ayos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix elements and the symmetry test {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"
msgstr "Matrix element at ang symmetry test {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A determinant is a sorted tuple of occupied qubit indices. Two determinants differing in more than\n"
"two occupied states have a vanishing matrix element; otherwise, the Slater-Condon rules give a short\n"
"sum over the interaction, multiplied by a fermionic sign counting how many occupied states lie between the\n"
"operators in the fixed register ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang determinant ay isang pinagsunod-sunod na tuple ng mga okupadong qubit index. Ang dalawang determinant na naiiba sa higit sa\n"
"dalawang okupadong state ay may matrix element na zero (naglalaho); kung hindi, ang mga Slater-Condon rule ay nagbibigay ng maikling\n"
"sum sa interaction, na pinarami ng isang fermionic sign na bumibilang kung ilang okupadong state ang nasa pagitan ng mga\n"
"operator sa nakapirming ayos ng register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`symmetry_allowed` is the integer test that all four exact quantum numbers reduce to. It is used both\n"
"to filter samples and to enumerate the exact basis for the runs small enough to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `symmetry_allowed` ay ang integer test na kinabubuuan ng lahat ng apat na eksaktong quantum number. Ginagamit ito parehong\n"
"upang i-filter ang mga sample at upang i-enumerate ang eksaktong basis para sa mga run na sapat kaliit upang suriin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference determinant {#the-reference-determinant}"
msgstr "Ang reference determinant {#the-reference-determinant}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ansatz is built on top of a single determinant, so that determinant should be the best one\n"
"available. Filling the lowest single-particle energies ignores the two-body interaction. In these model\n"
"spaces, that choice gives an energy 1–2 MeV above the lowest-energy determinant.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ansatz ay binuo sa ibabaw ng isang solong determinant, kaya dapat na ang determinant na iyon ang pinakamahusay na\n"
"mayroon. Ang pagpuno sa mga pinakamababang single-particle energy ay hindi isinasaalang-alang ang two-body interaction. Sa mga model\n"
"space na ito, ang pagpiling iyon ay nagbibigay ng energy na 1–2 MeV sa itaas ng determinant na may pinakamababang energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to fillings made of time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs forces $M_J = 0$ exactly and\n"
"leaves only $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per species (a few thousand at most), so the\n"
"best one can be found by searching them all on the full diagonal $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ties go to the most strongly aligned pairs, where the $J = 0$ pairing force is strongest. In every\n"
"case in this tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global\n"
"lowest-diagonal determinant, which is also the largest single component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paglilimita sa mga filling na binubuo ng time-reversed na $(+m_j, -m_j)$ na mga pares ay pumipilit sa $M_J = 0$ nang eksakto at\n"
"iniiwan lamang ang $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ na kandidato bawat species (ilang libo lang ang pinakamarami), kaya ang\n"
"pinakamahusay ay matatagpuan sa pamamagitan ng paghahanap sa lahat ng ito sa buong diagonal na $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ang mga tie ay napupunta sa mga pares na pinakamalakas na naka-align, kung saan pinakamalakas ang $J = 0$ pairing force. Sa bawat\n"
"kaso sa tutorial na ito na maaaring suriin laban sa isang buong enumeration, ibinabalik ng paghahanap ang global\n"
"na determinant na may pinakamababang diagonal, na siya ring pinakamalaking solong bahagi ng eksaktong ground state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The excitation pool and its perturbative ranking {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"
msgstr "Ang excitation pool at ang perturbative ranking nito {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Correlation is carried by two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) excitations from the reference. Two\n"
"selection rules reduce the pool before any circuit is built: an excitation must conserve $M_J$, and the hole pair and particle\n"
"pair must be able to couple to a common total $J$, which is a triangle inequality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dinadala ang correlation ng two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) na excitation mula sa reference. Dalawang\n"
"selection rule ang nagpapaliit sa pool bago mabuo ang anumang circuit: ang isang excitation ay dapat mag-conserve ng $M_J$, at ang hole pair at particle\n"
"pair ay dapat makapag-couple sa isang karaniwang kabuuang $J$, na isang triangle inequality.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remaining excitations are ranked by the Epstein-Nesbet second-order score of selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang natitirang mga excitation ay inaayos ayon sa Epstein-Nesbet second-order score ng selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which estimates how much correlation energy each excitation carries. The same two numbers fix the\n"
"circuit angle: with $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, the first-order amplitude\n"
"is $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. The [Appendix](#appendix) explains why the first-order amplitude is\n"
"the choice used in this tutorial rather than the exact two-level angle.\n"
msgstr ""
"na nagtatantya kung gaano karaming correlation energy ang dala ng bawat excitation. Ang parehong dalawang numero ang nagtatakda ng\n"
"circuit angle: gamit ang $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, ang first-order amplitude\n"
"ay $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. Ipinapaliwanag ng [Appendix](#appendix) kung bakit ang first-order amplitude ang\n"
"pinili sa tutorial na ito sa halip na ang eksaktong two-level angle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit-excitation blocks {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"
msgstr "Mga qubit-excitation block {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under the Jordan-Wigner mapping a particle-conserving $2p2h$ excitation operator becomes a sum of\n"
"eight Pauli strings, each carrying a string of $Z$ operators between the outermost indices. The\n"
"$Z$ strings enforce fermionic antisymmetry, and they are expensive: a proton-neutron\n"
"excitation spans the boundary between the two halves of the register and includes a parity string\n"
"across that boundary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa ilalim ng Jordan-Wigner mapping, ang isang particle-conserving na $2p2h$ excitation operator ay nagiging isang sum ng\n"
"walong Pauli string, bawat isa'y may dalang string ng mga $Z$ operator sa pagitan ng pinakalabas na indeks. Ang mga\n"
"$Z$ string ay nagpapatupad ng fermionic antisymmetry, at ang mga ito ay magastos: ang isang proton-neutron\n"
"excitation ay sumasaklaw sa hangganan sa pagitan ng dalawang kalahati ng register at may kasamang parity string\n"
"sa buong hangganang iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dropping the $Z$ strings gives the *qubit-excitation* operator of Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). The state prepared by this operator has different amplitudes, but it connects exactly the same pairs of determinants, so the set of determinants the circuit can\n"
"reach is unchanged. Pooled SQD uses these determinants for the classical diagonalization. Step 2 compares\n"
"the support of the two constructions and measures their hardware costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-alis sa mga $Z$ string ay nagbibigay ng *qubit-excitation* operator nina Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). Ang state na inihanda ng operator na ito ay may ibang amplitude, ngunit iniuugnay nito ang eksaktong parehong mga pares ng determinant, kaya ang set ng mga determinant na maaabot ng\n"
"circuit ay hindi nagbabago. Ginagamit ng Pooled SQD ang mga determinant na ito para sa classical diagonalization. Inihahambing ng Step 2\n"
"ang support ng dalawang konstruksyon at sinusukat ang kanilang hardware cost.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Building the Pauli form from $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, with the $Z$\n"
"string optional, keeps the two constructions a single flag apart. All eight terms of one generator\n"
"commute, so a single `PauliEvolutionGate` step is the exact exponential rather than a Trotter\n"
"approximation to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagbuo ng Pauli form mula sa $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, na may opsyonal na $Z$\n"
"string, ay nagpapanatili sa dalawang konstruksyon na iisang flag lamang ang pagkakaiba. Lahat ng walong termino ng isang generator ay\n"
"commute, kaya ang isang hakbang na `PauliEvolutionGate` ay ang eksaktong exponential sa halip na isang Trotter\n"
"approximation dito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The depth budget and the circuit ensemble {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"
msgstr "Ang depth budget at ang circuit ensemble {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single deep circuit containing every ranked excitation can exceed the hardware's coherence time. Spreading the pool\n"
"over an *ensemble* of shallow circuits and pooling their shots into one determinant set turns Step 2\n"
"into a packing problem: each excitation has a measured cost, each circuit has a budget, and the\n"
"question is how much of the ranked pool fits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang solong malalim na circuit na naglalaman ng bawat naka-rank na excitation ay maaaring lumampas sa coherence time ng hardware. Ang pagpapakalat ng pool\n"
"sa isang *ensemble* ng mababaw na mga circuit at ang pagsasama-sama ng kanilang mga shot sa isang set ng determinant ay ginagawang\n"
"packing problem ang Hakbang 2: bawat excitation ay may sinukat na cost, bawat circuit ay may budget, at ang\n"
"tanong ay kung gaano karami sa naka-rank na pool ang kasya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The budget is measured in **two-qubit depth** (layers of two-qubit gates on the critical path)\n"
"rather than in a raw gate count, because depth sets the circuit's duration and therefore how\n"
"much of the device's coherence it spends. The total count is reported alongside it, since that is the\n"
"better proxy for accumulated gate error; the two answer different questions and neither substitutes\n"
"for the other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang budget ay sinusukat sa **two-qubit depth** (mga layer ng two-qubit gate sa critical path)\n"
"sa halip na sa isang raw na bilang ng gate, dahil ang depth ang nagtatakda sa tagal ng circuit at samakatuwid\n"
"kung gaano karaming coherence ng device ang ginagastos nito. Iniuulat ang kabuuang bilang kasama nito, dahil iyon ang\n"
"mas mahusay na proxy para sa naipong gate error; ang dalawa ay sumasagot sa magkaibang tanong at hindi maaaring\n"
"palitan ang isa't isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both quantities are extracted by *arity*: an instruction acting on exactly two qubits, whatever the\n"
"backend happens to call its entangling gate. Matching on gate names instead could return zero\n"
"for an unfamiliar basis set, incorrectly placing the whole pool in one circuit without exceeding\n"
"the computed budget.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang parehong dami ay kinukuha ayon sa *arity*: isang instruction na kumikilos sa eksaktong dalawang qubit, anuman ang tawag ng\n"
"backend sa entangling gate nito. Ang pagtugma sa mga pangalan ng gate sa halip ay maaaring magbalik ng zero\n"
"para sa isang hindi pamilyar na basis set, na maling inilalagay ang buong pool sa isang circuit nang hindi lumalampas\n"
"sa nakalkulang budget.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Filling whichever circuit is currently emptiest, in rank order, keeps every circuit near the budget.\n"
"Costs are measured on the real backend target, one excitation at a time, because a cost read off an\n"
"abstract circuit is not the cost the transpiler produces.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagpuno kung alin man ang kasalukuyang pinakawalang laman na circuit, ayon sa rank order, ay pinapanatili ang bawat circuit malapit sa budget.\n"
"Sinusukat ang mga cost sa tunay na backend target, isang excitation sa isang pagkakataon, dahil ang cost na nabasa mula sa isang\n"
"abstract na circuit ay hindi ang cost na ginagawa ng transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing: repair, recombine, diagonalize {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"
msgstr "Post-processing: ayusin, pagsamahin muli, i-diagonalize {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three helpers do the work of Step 4.\n"
msgstr "Tatlong helper ang gumagawa ng trabaho ng Step 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`half_configurations` splits each sampled row into a proton half and a neutron half, and keeps each\n"
"half that has the correct nucleon number. A row with a valid proton half contributes that half even if its\n"
"neutron half has the wrong nucleon number. Each half carries the total sampled weight of the rows it appeared in, which\n"
"is what ranks it if the subspace needs to be truncated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hinahati ng `half_configurations` ang bawat na-sample na row sa isang proton half at isang neutron half, at pinapanatili ang bawat\n"
"half na may tamang nucleon number. Ang isang row na may valid na proton half ay nag-aambag ng half na iyon kahit na ang\n"
"neutron half nito ay may maling nucleon number. Ang bawat half ay may dalang kabuuang sampled weight ng mga row kung saan ito lumitaw, na\n"
"siyang nagra-rank dito kung kailangang putulin ang subspace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`grow_subspace` recombines the halves into every product that lands in the target $M_J$ and parity\n"
"sector, *adding* to the subspace it is given rather than rebuilding it. That keeps successive\n"
"subspaces nested, which is what makes the energy sequence monotone non-increasing instead of merely\n"
"fluctuating around a bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinagsasama-sama muli ng `grow_subspace` ang mga half sa bawat produkto na napupunta sa target na $M_J$ at parity\n"
"sector, *idinadagdag* ito sa subspace na ibinigay dito sa halip na muling buuin ito. Nagpapanatili iyon sa magkakasunod na\n"
"subspace na naka-nest, na siyang dahilan kung bakit ang energy sequence ay monotone non-increasing sa halip na basta na lang\n"
"umiindayog sa paligid ng isang bound.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`recovery_loop` is the self-consistent configuration recovery of the pooled SQD paper\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): repair the two half-register nucleon numbers against the current occupancy\n"
"estimate, recombine, diagonalize, and take the next occupancy estimate from the eigenvector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `recovery_loop` ay ang self-consistent configuration recovery ng pooled SQD paper\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): ayusin ang dalawang half-register nucleon number laban sa kasalukuyang pagtatantya ng occupancy,\n"
"pagsamahin muli, i-diagonalize, at kunin ang susunod na pagtatantya ng occupancy mula sa eigenvector.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check the bit-ordering conventions carefully to avoid incorrect results. `qiskit-addon-sqd` writes column 0 of its\n"
"bitstring matrix as the *highest* qubit index, so reversing a row gives occupation indexed by qubit;\n"
"its \"right\" half is the low qubit indices, which is the proton block. Correspondingly,\n"
"`recover_configurations` takes `num_elec_a` as the proton number and average occupancies ordered\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` by qubit index. The addon assumes bit $i$ pairs with bit $i + N$; in this\n"
"register, proton qubit $i$ and neutron qubit $i + N$ are the same $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ state, so the\n"
"assumption is physically meaningful here rather than incidental.\n"
msgstr ""
"Suriing mabuti ang mga convention ng bit-ordering upang maiwasan ang maling resulta. Isinusulat ng `qiskit-addon-sqd` ang column 0 ng\n"
"bitstring matrix nito bilang ang *pinakamataas* na qubit index, kaya ang pagbaligtad sa isang row ay nagbibigay ng occupation na indexed ayon sa qubit;\n"
"ang \"right\" na half nito ay ang mababang qubit index, na siyang proton block. Kaugnay nito,\n"
"kinukuha ng `recover_configurations` ang `num_elec_a` bilang proton number at ang average occupancies ay inaayos\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` ayon sa qubit index. Ipinapalagay ng addon na ang bit $i$ ay nagpapares sa bit $i + N$; sa\n"
"register na ito, ang proton qubit $i$ at neutron qubit $i + N$ ay parehong $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ na state, kaya\n"
"makabuluhan ang pagpapalagay na ito dito sa pisikal na paraan sa halip na aksidente lamang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend, budget, and run parameters {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"
msgstr "Backend, budget, at run parameters {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every run that follows uses the same backend, the same pass managers, and the same depth budget, so the three\n"
"are directly comparable. The budget ties them together: every circuit in every\n"
"ensemble has to fit inside it, and it decides how much of a pool can be sampled at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat run na susunod ay gumagamit ng parehong backend, parehong pass manager, at parehong depth budget, kaya ang tatlo\n"
"ay direktang maihahambing. Pinagbubuklod sila ng budget: ang bawat circuit sa bawat\n"
"ensemble ay kailangang magkasya dito, at ito ang nagpapasiya kung gaano karami sa isang pool ang maaaring ma-sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The values here were chosen by measuring transpiled cost against a Heron target. At a two-qubit depth of 300 and 16 circuits, both 24-qubit and 40-qubit ensembles come out well under 100 microseconds per\n"
"circuit, against coherence times of a few hundred microseconds. Increasing the budget includes more of the pool but increases circuit duration. Measure this\n"
"tradeoff for your backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinili ang mga halaga dito sa pamamagitan ng pagsukat ng transpiled cost laban sa isang Heron target. Sa two-qubit depth na 300 at 16 circuit, ang parehong 24-qubit at 40-qubit na ensemble ay lumalabas nang malayong mas mababa sa 100 microseconds bawat\n"
"circuit, laban sa coherence time na ilang daang microseconds. Ang pagdaragdag ng budget ay nagsasama ng higit pa sa pool ngunit nagpapataas ng tagal ng circuit. Sukatin ang\n"
"tradeoff na ito para sa iyong backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale hardware example {#small-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng hardware sa maliit na sukat {#small-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section follows the four-step workflow on a QPU, using the same backend and the same\n"
"gate budget as the large-scale runs. The smaller problem provides an exact reference for checking the result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinusundan ng seksyong ito ang apat na hakbang na workflow sa isang QPU, gamit ang parehong backend at parehong\n"
"gate budget gaya ng mga large-scale run. Ang mas maliit na problema ay nagbibigay ng isang eksaktong reference para sa pagsuri sa resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The small-scale problem is $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: two valence protons and two valence neutrons in the\n"
"$sd$ shell above an $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$ core, with the USDA interaction [\\[2\\]](#references). Three\n"
"orbitals per species give 24 qubits, and the complete symmetry-allowed basis is 640 determinants,\n"
"small enough to compare the energy estimates with the exact answer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang small-scale na problema ay $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: dalawang valence proton at dalawang valence neutron sa\n"
"$sd$ shell sa ibabaw ng isang $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$ core, gamit ang USDA interaction [\\[2\\]](#references). Tatlong\n"
"orbital bawat species ang nagbibigay ng 24 qubit, at ang kumpletong symmetry-allowed na basis ay 640 determinant,\n"
"maliit na sapat upang ihambing ang mga pagtatantya ng energy sa eksaktong sagot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang classical inputs sa isang quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Read the interaction, build the register, and construct the reference determinant. The following table shows the register information from the [Background](#background), read directly\n"
"from the interaction file.\n"
msgstr ""
"Basahin ang interaction, buuin ang register, at bumuo ng reference determinant. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na talahanayan ang impormasyon ng register mula sa [Background](#background), na binasa nang direkta\n"
"mula sa interaction file.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run two checks on the Hamiltonian before continuing. Both are inexpensive and can reveal\n"
"recoupling errors that a single energy calculation might not detect.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsagawa ng dalawang check sa Hamiltonian bago magpatuloy. Parehong mura at maaaring maglantad ng\n"
"mga recoupling error na maaaring hindi matukoy ng isang solong energy calculation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A rotationally invariant Hamiltonian organizes its eigenstates into $J$ multiplets, so every\n"
"eigenvalue of the $M_J = 2$ sector must also appear in the $M_J = 0$ spectrum at the same energy. The gap between the ground state and the lowest state carrying $M_J = 2$ is the $2^+$ excitation\n"
"energy, which is measured: $1.634$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). An empirical\n"
"$sd$-shell interaction is expected to agree within a few hundred keV.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inaayos ng isang rotationally invariant na Hamiltonian ang mga eigenstate nito sa $J$ multiplets, kaya ang bawat\n"
"eigenvalue ng $M_J = 2$ sector ay dapat ding lumitaw sa $M_J = 0$ spectrum sa parehong energy. Ang puwang sa pagitan ng ground state at ng pinakamababang state na may dalang $M_J = 2$ ay ang $2^+$ excitation\n"
"energy, na sinukat: $1.634$ MeV para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). Inaasahang sasang-ayon ang isang empirical\n"
"$sd$-shell interaction sa loob ng ilang daang keV.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, construct the operator pool. Applying the two selection rules gives an important result: for this reference, in this model space, **there are no allowed single excitations at all**.\n"
msgstr "Sunod, buuin ang operator pool. Ang paglalapat ng dalawang selection rule ay nagbibigay ng mahalagang resulta: para sa reference na ito, sa model space na ito, **wala talagang pinapayagang single excitation**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A $1p1h$ excitation conserves $M_J$ only if the particle state\n"
"has the same $m_j$ as the hole. The reference occupies the two states of largest $|m_j|$ in the\n"
"lowest orbital ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ of $0d_{5/2}$), and no other orbital in the $sd$ shell reaches\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, since $0d_{3/2}$ stops at $3/2$ and $1s_{1/2}$ at $1/2$. Therefore, no single excitation\n"
"survives, and correlation is carried entirely by $2p2h$ excitations. This is a property of the\n"
"reference and the shell, not a general law; the following cell counts it rather than assuming it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang $1p1h$ excitation ay nag-co-conserve ng $M_J$ lamang kung ang particle state ay\n"
"may parehong $m_j$ gaya ng hole. Ino-okupa ng reference ang dalawang state na may pinakamalaking $|m_j|$ sa\n"
"pinakamababang orbital ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ ng $0d_{5/2}$), at walang ibang orbital sa $sd$ shell ang umaabot sa\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, dahil ang $0d_{3/2}$ ay hanggang $3/2$ lamang at ang $1s_{1/2}$ ay hanggang $1/2$. Samakatuwid, walang single excitation\n"
"ang nakaligtas, at ang correlation ay dala nang buo ng mga $2p2h$ excitation. Ito ay isang katangian ng\n"
"reference at ng shell, hindi isang pangkalahatang batas; ang sumusunod na cell ay binibilang ito sa halip na ipagpalagay lamang ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatupad sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpilation reveals the hardware cost of the Jordan-Wigner $Z$ strings and the savings from\n"
"using qubit excitations. The first cell measures both constructions against the real backend\n"
"target and checks the claim, introduced in the [Setup](#setup), that dropping the $Z$ strings changes the\n"
"amplitudes but not the set of determinants the circuit can reach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilalantad ng transpilation ang hardware cost ng Jordan-Wigner $Z$ strings at ang matitipid mula sa\n"
"paggamit ng qubit excitations. Sinusukat ng unang cell ang parehong konstruksyon laban sa tunay na backend\n"
"target at sinusuri ang claim, na ipinakilala sa [Setup](#setup), na ang pag-alis sa $Z$ strings ay nagbabago sa\n"
"amplitudes ngunit hindi sa set ng mga determinant na maaabot ng circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare two consequences of this substitution. A qubit excitation costs the same regardless of the distance between its\n"
"indices, so proton-neutron excitations, which span the boundary between the two halves of the\n"
"register and make up most of the pool, no longer have this additional cost. The whole pool then\n"
"fits inside the budget, which means the limit on the result is sampling rather than circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ihambing ang dalawang bunga ng pagpapalit na ito. Ang isang qubit excitation ay may parehong gastos anuman ang distansya sa pagitan ng mga\n"
"index nito, kaya ang mga proton-neutron excitation, na sumasaklaw sa hangganan sa pagitan ng dalawang kalahati ng\n"
"register at bumubuo sa karamihan ng pool, ay wala nang karagdagang gastos na ito. Ang buong pool ay\n"
"kasya na ngayon sa loob ng budget, na nangangahulugang ang limitasyon sa resulta ay ang sampling sa halip na ang circuit depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Isagawa gamit ang Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Submit one job per problem, with the whole ensemble as a single list of circuits. Gate and\n"
"measurement twirling and dynamical decoupling are enabled to reduce the effects of hardware noise.\n"
"Their benefit depends on the circuit and backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsumite ng isang job bawat problema, kasama ang buong ensemble bilang iisang listahan ng mga circuit. Pinapagana ang gate at\n"
"measurement twirling at dynamical decoupling upang mabawasan ang epekto ng hardware noise.\n"
"Depende ang kanilang benepisyo sa circuit at backend.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each job's ID is printed. Use `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` to retrieve the completed job and its\n"
"results without using additional QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Naka-print ang ID ng bawat job. Gamitin ang `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` upang kunin ang nakumpletong job at ang mga\n"
"resulta nito nang hindi gumagamit ng karagdagang QPU time.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa gustong classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Convert the quantum samples into an energy estimate using the nuclear-symmetry constraints\n"
"described in the [Background](#background) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-convert ang quantum samples papunta sa energy estimate gamit ang nuclear-symmetry constraints\n"
"na inilarawan sa seksyon ng [Background](#background).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration recovery repairs the two nucleon numbers.** `recover_configurations` takes each shot that\n"
"has the wrong number of protons or neutrons and flips the bits least consistent with the current\n"
"estimate of the average orbital occupancies, instead of discarding it. On the first pass the\n"
"occupancy estimate comes from the shots that already survived; afterward it comes from the\n"
"eigenvector of the previous subspace, which makes the procedure self-consistent.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Inaayos ng configuration recovery ang dalawang nucleon number.** Kinukuha ng `recover_configurations` ang bawat shot na\n"
"may maling bilang ng proton o neutron at binabaligtad ang mga bit na pinakahindi tugma sa kasalukuyang\n"
"estimate ng average orbital occupancy, sa halip na itapon ito. Sa unang pass, ang\n"
"estimate ng occupancy ay galing sa mga shot na nakaligtas na; pagkatapos, ito ay galing sa\n"
"eigenvector ng naunang subspace, na siyang gumagawa sa proseso na self-consistent.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**$M_J$ and parity are imposed on the recombined products, not on whole shots.** Every repaired shot\n"
"contributes a proton half and a neutron half, and the subspace is spanned by every product of a\n"
"sampled proton configuration with a sampled neutron configuration that lands at $M_J = 0$ with the\n"
"right parity. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ instead would throw away two good halves for the\n"
"sake of a quantum number that belongs to their combination.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ipinapataw ang $M_J$ at parity sa mga pinagsamang produkto, hindi sa buong shot.** Bawat inayos na shot ay\n"
"nag-aambag ng kalahati para sa proton at kalahati para sa neutron, at ang subspace ay sinasaklaw ng bawat produkto ng isang\n"
"na-sample na proton configuration kasama ang isang na-sample na neutron configuration na nagreresulta sa $M_J = 0$ na may\n"
"tamang parity. Ang pag-filter ng buong shot batay sa total $M_J$ ay magtatapon ng dalawang mabuting kalahati para lamang sa\n"
"isang quantum number na kabilang sa kanilang kombinasyon.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four quantum-number checks reject different fractions of samples. The two nucleon numbers\n"
"account for most of the filtering. Parity is *automatically* satisfied inside a single major shell: every $sd$ orbital\n"
"has even $\\ell$ and every $pf$ orbital odd $\\ell$, so once the nucleon numbers are right the parity\n"
"cannot be wrong. The parity check is retained because a cross-shell model space would make it an\n"
"independent constraint. The $M_J$ check keeps products in the target angular-momentum sector. The value of\n"
"having four exact quantum numbers is that they are *cheap and exact*, not that each one is a large\n"
"filter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iba-ibang porsyento ng samples ang tinatanggihan ng apat na quantum-number checks. Ang dalawang nucleon number\n"
"ang bumubuo sa karamihan ng filtering. Ang parity ay *awtomatikong* nasusunod sa loob ng iisang major shell: bawat $sd$ orbital\n"
"ay may even $\\ell$ at bawat $pf$ orbital ay odd $\\ell$, kaya kapag tama na ang nucleon numbers, hindi na maaaring\n"
"mali ang parity. Pinapanatili pa rin ang parity check dahil ang isang cross-shell model space ay gagawin itong\n"
"independent constraint. Pinapanatili ng $M_J$ check ang mga produkto sa target angular-momentum sector. Ang pakinabang ng\n"
"pagkakaroon ng apat na eksaktong quantum number ay dahil *mura at eksakto* ang mga ito, hindi dahil malaking\n"
"filter ang bawat isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Diagonalizing gives a variational upper bound.** Because each iteration's subspace contains the\n"
"last, the sequence of energies falls monotonically, and every entry in it is a rigorous upper bound on\n"
"the true ground-state energy, regardless of the noise in the samples that produced it.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nagbibigay ang diagonalization ng variational upper bound.** Dahil ang subspace ng bawat iteration ay naglalaman ng\n"
"nauna, monotonically bumababa ang sequence ng energies, at bawat entry dito ay isang rigorous upper bound sa\n"
"tunay na ground-state energy, kahit anuman ang noise sa samples na nagbunga nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the results {#evaluate-the-results}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga resulta {#evaluate-the-results}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the following checks to evaluate your results on a Heron-class backend with these settings:\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang mga sumusunod na check para suriin ang iyong mga resulta sa isang Heron-class backend gamit ang mga settings na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Shot survival** on the two nucleon numbers measures the fraction of shots with the correct proton and neutron counts. It can fall as\n"
"the register grows. A survival rate near zero can indicate a problem with circuit execution. Check the ISA depth in Step 2 and the backend's calibration, not the post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang shot survival** sa dalawang nucleon number ay sumusukat sa porsyento ng mga shot na may tamang bilang ng proton at neutron. Maaari itong bumaba habang\n"
"lumalaki ang register. Ang survival rate na malapit sa zero ay maaaring senyales ng problema sa circuit execution. Suriin ang ISA depth sa Hakbang 2 at ang calibration ng backend, hindi ang post-processing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovery loop** should print a subspace dimension that stays constant or grows and an energy that stays constant or falls with\n"
"each iteration. If iteration 1 already reaches `MAX_DIMENSION`, the classical solver rather than the\n"
"sampling is the binding constraint.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang recovery loop** ay dapat mag-print ng subspace dimension na nananatiling pareho o lumalaki at energy na nananatiling pareho o bumababa sa\n"
"bawat iteration. Kung ang iteration 1 ay naabot na agad ang `MAX_DIMENSION`, ang classical solver sa halip na ang\n"
"sampling ang siyang binding constraint.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovered fraction** for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ should be high, because the ansatz ceiling\n"
"computed in Step 1 is the full 640-determinant space; this run is where sampling, not\n"
"expressiveness, is the only obstacle.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang na-recover na porsyento** para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ ay dapat mataas, dahil ang ansatz ceiling\n"
"na kinalkula sa Hakbang 1 ay ang buong 640-determinant space; sa run na ito, ang sampling, hindi ang\n"
"expressiveness, ang tanging hadlang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The two assertions** in the preceding cell check the variational bounds. A bound that rises means the\n"
"subspaces stopped being nested, and a bound below the exact energy means something is wrong with the\n"
"Hamiltonian, not with the hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang dalawang assertion** sa naunang cell ay sumusuri sa variational bounds. Kung tumaas ang bound, ibig sabihin\n"
"ay hindi na naka-nested ang mga subspace, at kung ang bound ay mas mababa sa eksaktong energy, may mali sa\n"
"Hamiltonian, hindi sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Counterintuitively, a *noisier* backend can give a slightly better bound than a clean one, because\n"
"errors produce valid half-configurations the ideal circuit would never have sampled, and widening\n"
"a variational subspace cannot raise its lowest eigenvalue. Noisy simulation can demonstrate the same effect; this tutorial shows it with\n"
"hardware samples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagama't kakaiba, ang isang *maingay* na backend ay maaaring magbigay ng bahagyang mas magandang bound kaysa sa isang malinis, dahil\n"
"nagbubunga ang mga error ng mga valid half-configuration na hindi kailanman ma-sa-sample ng ideal na circuit, at ang pagpapalawak\n"
"ng variational subspace ay hindi maaaring magpataas ng pinakamababang eigenvalue nito. Maaaring ipakita ng noisy simulation ang parehong epekto; ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito gamit ang\n"
"hardware samples.\n"

