# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: beyond the tutorial's exact-diagonalization capacity {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"
msgstr "$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$: lampas sa kapasidad ng eksaktong diagonalization ng tutorial {#48mathrmcr-beyond-the-tutorials-exact-diagonalization-capacity}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adding two protons and two neutrons uses the same 40-qubit register (`4, 4` for\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) and increases the basis size by a factor of about 491, to 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinants. That\n"
"matrix is far beyond anything this tutorial will build, so `exact=False`: there is no exact reference energy,\n"
"only the variational bound and the reference determinant it improves on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagdaragdag ng dalawang proton at dalawang neutron ay gumagamit ng parehong 40-qubit na register (`4, 4` para sa\n"
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$) at pinapataas ang laki ng basis nang halos 491 beses, sa 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinant. Ang\n"
"matrix na iyon ay malayong-malayo sa kahit anong bubuuin ng tutorial na ito, kaya `exact=False`: walang eksaktong reference energy,\n"
"kundi ang variational bound lamang at ang reference determinant na pinabuti nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two things change at this scale, and both are visible in the printout. The pool grows to several\n"
"hundred allowed excitations, so the fixed gate budget now covers a minority of it rather than all of\n"
"it. Also, the product subspace the samples span is larger than `MAX_DIMENSION`, so the dense solver\n"
"truncates it by sampled weight. The bound remains rigorous but can be less accurate than a bound\n"
"computed from all the sampled configurations. A production calculation would retain the samples\n"
"and use a solver that supports a larger subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"May dalawang bagay na nagbabago sa sukat na ito, at parehong nakikita sa printout. Lumalaki ang pool sa\n"
"ilang daang allowed excitation, kaya ang fixed gate budget ay sumasaklaw na lamang ng minorya nito sa halip na lahat\n"
"nito. Gayundin, ang product subspace na sinasaklaw ng samples ay mas malaki kaysa sa `MAX_DIMENSION`, kaya\n"
"tinatapyas ito ng dense solver ayon sa sampled weight. Nananatiling rigorous ang bound pero maaaring hindi kasingtumpak ng bound na\n"
"kinalkula mula sa lahat ng sampled configuration. Ang production calculation ay pananatilihin ang samples\n"
"at gagamit ng solver na sumusuporta sa mas malaking subspace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate a result without an exact reference {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"
msgstr "Suriin ang resulta na walang eksaktong reference {#evaluate-a-result-without-an-exact-reference}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ run has no exact reference within this tutorial. Use the existing samples\n"
"to assess convergence and compare with the classical selection baseline, without additional QPU\n"
"time or full-space diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang run ng $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ ay walang eksaktong reference sa loob ng tutorial na ito. Gamitin ang mga umiiral na sample\n"
"para suriin ang convergence at ikumpara sa classical selection baseline, nang walang dagdag na QPU\n"
"time o full-space diagonalization.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Is it converged?** Reorder the retained determinants by their weight in the converged eigenvector\n"
"and the subspaces become *nested*, so diagonalizing the leading $d \\times d$ block for a ladder of $d$\n"
"traces the bound's descent across two decades of subspace size. If it is still falling steeply at the\n"
"largest $d$, the classical solver's dimension cap is the binding constraint and `MAX_DIMENSION` is the\n"
"parameter to increase. If it has flattened, adding more of the retained determinants offers little improvement;\n"
"further progress may require sampling additional configurations. The\n"
"Hamiltonian is built once at full size and every rung is a principal block of it, so the whole\n"
"sweep costs one matrix build rather than one per rung.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Nakumberhe na ba ito?** Kung i-reorder ang mga natirang determinant ayon sa kanilang weight sa nakumberhe nang eigenvector,\n"
"magiging *nested* ang mga subspace, kaya ang pag-diagonalize sa nangungunang $d \\times d$ block para sa isang hagdan na may $d$\n"
"ay sinusundan ang pagbaba ng bound sa dalawang order of magnitude ng laki ng subspace. Kung matarik pa itong bumababa sa\n"
"pinakamalaking $d$, ang dimension cap ng classical solver ang binding constraint at `MAX_DIMENSION` ang\n"
"parameter na dapat dagdagan. Kung patag na ito, kaunti lang ang maidudulot ng dagdag na natirang determinant;\n"
"maaaring kailanganin ang pag-sample ng karagdagang configuration para sa karagdagang progreso. Ang\n"
"Hamiltonian ay binubuo isang beses sa buong laki at bawat rung ay isang principal block nito, kaya ang buong\n"
"sweep ay nagkakahalaga ng isang matrix build sa halip na isa bawat rung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**How does quantum sampling compare with classical selection?** Compare with a subspace of the\n"
"same size chosen by the classical selection procedure: take the pool ranked by perturbation theory in score\n"
"order, grow the product subspace to the same dimension, and diagonalize that instead. Both curves are\n"
"rigorous upper bounds on the same Hamiltonian, so whichever sits lower at equal dimension picked the\n"
"better determinants. This comparison decides whether hardware sampling improves the energy estimate\n"
"relative to this classical baseline.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Paano ihahambing ang quantum sampling sa classical selection?** Ikumpara sa isang subspace ng\n"
"parehong laki na napili ng classical selection procedure: kunin ang pool na naka-rank ayon sa perturbation theory sa score\n"
"order, palakihin ang product subspace sa parehong dimension, at i-diagonalize iyon sa halip. Parehong curve ay\n"
"rigorous upper bound sa parehong Hamiltonian, kaya kung alin man ang mas mababa sa parehong dimension ang pumili ng\n"
"mas magandang determinant. Ang paghahambing na ito ang magpapasya kung pinapabuti ng hardware sampling ang energy estimate\n"
"kumpara sa classical baseline na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This subspace is not selected for excited states. Configuration recovery steers the subspace\n"
"using ground-state occupancies, so the higher eigenvalues are much further from converged than the\n"
"lowest one, and the first excitation energy comes out well above the measured $2^+$. Reaching excited\n"
"states properly needs a subspace selected for them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi napili ang subspace na ito para sa excited states. Ginagabayan ng configuration recovery ang subspace\n"
"gamit ang ground-state occupancies, kaya ang mga mas mataas na eigenvalue ay mas malayo pa sa convergence kaysa sa\n"
"pinakamababa, at ang unang excitation energy ay lumalabas na mas mataas kaysa sa sinusukat na $2^+$. Para maabot nang maayos ang excited\n"
"states, kailangan ng subspace na piniling talaga para dito.\n"

