# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background (Fortran) {#background-fortran}"
msgstr "Batayan (Fortran) {#background-fortran}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The nuclear shell model treats a nucleus as a few *valence* nucleons moving in a small set of single-particle orbitals above an inert *core*, interacting through an empirical two-body force fitted to measured spectra. Its computational cost is combinatorial: the basis is every way of distributing the valence protons and neutrons over the available states, and this growth limits the model spaces accessible to exact diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinitingnan ng nuclear shell model ang isang nucleus bilang ilang *valence* na nucleon na gumagalaw sa isang maliit na set ng\n"
"single-particle orbital sa ibabaw ng isang inert na *core*, na nag-iinteraksyon sa pamamagitan ng isang empirical two-body force\n"
"na in-fit sa mga sinukat na spectra. Ang computational cost nito ay\n"
"combinatorial: ang basis ay bawat paraan ng pamamahagi ng valence protons at neutrons sa mga\n"
"magagamit na state, at ang paglagong ito ang naglilimita sa mga model space na naaabot ng exact diagonalization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooled sample-based quantum diagonalization (pooled SQD) [\\[1\\]](#references) splits that problem in two. A quantum circuit is used only to *propose* which basis states matter. It is measured in the computational basis, and each measured bitstring names one Slater determinant. The Hamiltonian is then built and diagonalized classically in the span of those determinants. Because the classical step is an exact diagonalization inside a subspace, it returns a variational upper bound on the true ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hinahati ng Pooled sample-based quantum diagonalization (pooled SQD) [\\[1\\]](#references) ang problemang iyon sa dalawa. Ang isang\n"
"quantum circuit ay ginagamit lamang upang *magmungkahi* kung aling mga basis state ang mahalaga. Ito ay sinusukat sa\n"
"computational basis, at ang bawat nasukat na bitstring ay nagpapangalan sa isang Slater determinant. Ang Hamiltonian ay\n"
"pagkatapos ay binubuo at dina-diagonalize nang classical sa span ng mga determinant na iyon. Dahil ang classical\n"
"na hakbang ay isang eksaktong diagonalization sa loob ng isang subspace, nagbabalik ito ng isang variational upper bound\n"
"sa tunay na ground-state energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise changes *which* determinants the circuit proposes, but it does not enter the classical Hamiltonian. A shot that violates a conserved quantity is discarded, and a shot that survives is a legitimate basis vector however it was produced. Noise therefore costs subspace quality, not correctness. Nuclear structure provides several exact quantum numbers for this check: a physical determinant must carry the right number of valence protons *and* valence neutrons, the right total angular-momentum projection $M_J$, and the right parity.\n"
msgstr "Binabago ng noise *kung aling* mga determinant ang iminumungkahi ng circuit, ngunit hindi ito pumapasok sa classical na Hamiltonian. Itinatapon ang isang shot na lumalabag sa isang conserved quantity, at ang isang shot na nakaligtas ay isang lehitimong basis vector kahit paano ito nabuo. Kaya ang noise ay nakakaapekto sa kalidad ng subspace, hindi sa kawastuhan. Nagbibigay ang nuclear structure ng ilang eksaktong quantum number para sa pagsusuring ito: ang isang pisikal na determinant ay dapat may tamang bilang ng valence proton *at* valence neutron, tamang total angular-momentum projection $M_J$, at tamang parity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran application uses the same register as the Python example. Every qubit is one $m$-scheme single-particle state $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, and $|1\\rangle$ means occupied. Protons come first, then neutrons; within a species, orbitals follow the order of the interaction file; within an orbital, $m_j$ descends. The $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ example here uses this 24-qubit $sd$-shell register.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng Fortran application ang parehong register gaya ng Python na halimbawa. Ang bawat qubit ay isang $m$-scheme single-particle state $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, at ang $|1\\rangle$ ay nangangahulugang occupied. Mauuna ang mga proton, saka ang mga neutron; sa loob ng isang species, sinusunod ng mga orbital ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng interaction file; sa loob ng isang orbital, bumababa ang $m_j$. Ginagamit ng halimbawang $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ dito ang 24-qubit na $sd$-shell register na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian is a one-body term plus a two-body interaction,\n"
msgstr "Ang Hamiltonian ay isang one-body term kasama ang isang two-body interaction,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $p,q,r,s$ label $m$-scheme states. The interaction file tabulates two-body matrix elements in the $J$-coupled basis of orbitals, and the application recovers each $m$-scheme element $\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle$ by Clebsch-Gordan recoupling. The regression test in [Check the workflow locally](#check-the-workflow-locally) confirms that this produces the same Hamiltonian as the Python example.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $p,q,r,s$ ay tumutukoy sa mga $m$-scheme state. Itinatala ng interaction file ang mga two-body matrix element sa $J$-coupled na basis ng mga orbital, at nakukuha ng application ang bawat $m$-scheme na element na $\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle$ sa pamamagitan ng Clebsch-Gordan recoupling. Kinukumpirma ng regression test sa [Check the workflow locally](#check-the-workflow-locally) na gumagawa ito ng parehong Hamiltonian gaya ng Python na halimbawa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran workflow {#the-fortran-workflow}"
msgstr "Ang Fortran workflow {#the-fortran-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reference determinant.** Fill the lowest single-particle-energy $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs of each species, which gives $M_J = 0$.\n"
msgstr "**Reference determinant.** Punuin ang mga pares na $(+m_j, -m_j)$ na may pinakamababang single-particle energy ng bawat species, na nagbibigay ng $M_J = 0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Excitation pool.** Generate the single and double excitations of the reference allowed by angular-momentum coupling, rank them by a second-order perturbation-theory score, $V^2/|\\Delta|$, and seed each with its two-level mixing angle.\n"
msgstr "**Excitation pool.** Buuin ang mga single at double excitation ng reference na pinapayagan ng angular-momentum coupling, i-rank ang mga ito ayon sa second-order perturbation-theory score, $V^2/|\\Delta|$, at lagyan ang bawat isa ng two-level mixing angle nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuit ensemble.** Each circuit prepares the reference and applies the next slice of the ranked pool: Givens rotations for single excitations and qubit-excitation gates for double excitations. With the default of 16 excitations per circuit, 11 circuits cover the whole double-excitation pool for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$.\n"
msgstr "**Circuit ensemble.** Inihahanda ng bawat circuit ang reference at inilalapat ang susunod na slice ng ranked pool: Givens rotations para sa single excitations at qubit-excitation gates para sa double excitations. Sa default na 16 excitations bawat circuit, sakop ng 11 circuits ang buong double-excitation pool para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sample.** Transpile each circuit and sample it on a QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Sample.** I-transpile ang bawat circuit at i-sample ito sa isang QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Filter.** Keep only shots with the right proton number, neutron number, $M_J$, and parity, and discard the rest.\n"
msgstr "**Filter.** Panatilihin lang ang mga shot na may tamang proton number, neutron number, $M_J$, at parity, at itapon ang iba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Diagonalize.** Build the Hamiltonian in the span of the unique kept determinants, pooled across all circuits, and diagonalize it with LAPACK to get a variational upper bound. Alternatively, diagonalize each circuit's samples separately.\n"
msgstr "**Diagonalize.** Buuin ang Hamiltonian sa span ng mga natatanging napanatiling determinant, pinagsama mula sa lahat ng circuit, at i-diagonalize ito gamit ang LAPACK para makakuha ng variational upper bound. Bilang alternatibo, i-diagonalize nang hiwalay ang mga sample ng bawat circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each step maps to a source file in the Fortran directory:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat hakbang ay tumutugma sa isang source file sa Fortran directory:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Step | Source |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Read the interaction and recouple to the $m$-scheme | `physics/usdb_reader.f90`, `physics/clebsch_gordan.f90`, `physics/orbital_registry.f90` |\n"
"| Rank and seed the excitation pool | `nuclear_pool.f90`, `nuclear_selection.f90` |\n"
"| Build the circuits | `circuit/nuclear_ansatz.f90`, `nuclear_gates.f90` |\n"
"| Sample, filter, and diagonalize | `circuit/nuclear_shell_driver.f90`, `physics/symmetry_filter.f90`, `physics/exact_solver.f90` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Hakbang | Source |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Basahin ang interaction at i-recouple sa $m$-scheme | `physics/usdb_reader.f90`, `physics/clebsch_gordan.f90`, `physics/orbital_registry.f90` |\n"
"| I-rank at i-seed ang excitation pool | `nuclear_pool.f90`, `nuclear_selection.f90` |\n"
"| Buuin ang mga circuit | `circuit/nuclear_ansatz.f90`, `nuclear_gates.f90` |\n"
"| Mag-sample, mag-filter, at mag-diagonalize | `circuit/nuclear_shell_driver.f90`, `physics/symmetry_filter.f90`, `physics/exact_solver.f90` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran workflow differs from the Python example in several choices, such as how it picks the reference determinant and how it handles samples with the wrong symmetry. [Differences from the Python example](#differences-from-the-python-example) lists them.\n"
msgstr "Iba ang Fortran workflow sa Python example sa ilang pagpili, tulad ng kung paano nito pinipili ang reference determinant at kung paano nito hinahawakan ang mga sample na may maling symmetry. Nakalista ang mga ito sa [Mga pagkakaiba mula sa Python example](#differences-from-the-python-example).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements (Fortran) {#requirements-fortran}"
msgstr "Mga Kinakailangan (Fortran) {#requirements-fortran}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This implementation is adapted from the nuclear shell-model application in [qiskit-fortran](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fortran), the Fortran bindings for Qiskit. Build and run the version in the Fortran directory linked in the preceding note rather than the upstream application, because it includes corrections to interaction mass scaling and antisymmetrized pair-exchange phases.\n"
msgstr "Ang implementasyong ito ay hango sa nuclear shell-model application sa [qiskit-fortran](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fortran), ang mga Fortran binding para sa Qiskit. I-build at patakbuhin ang bersyon sa Fortran directory na naka-link sa naunang tala sa halip na ang upstream application, dahil kasama rito ang mga pagwawasto sa interaction mass scaling at sa antisymmetrized pair-exchange phases.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow the [build instructions](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/nuclear_sqd_pooled/fortran/BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md) to build the Qiskit C library, the Fortran bindings, and this application. The build instructions set `NUCLEAR_SRC` to the Fortran directory and `NUCLEAR_DEPS` to a separate directory for the dependencies; the commands in this example use those variables. Use the same Fortran compiler for the bindings and the application, because module files are compiler-specific. Building the Qiskit C library (`make c`) takes several minutes.\n"
msgstr "Sundin ang [mga tagubilin sa pag-build](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/nuclear_sqd_pooled/fortran/BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md) para i-build ang Qiskit C library, ang mga Fortran binding, at ang application na ito. Itinatakda ng mga tagubilin sa pag-build ang `NUCLEAR_SRC` sa Fortran directory at ang `NUCLEAR_DEPS` sa hiwalay na directory para sa mga dependency; ginagamit ng mga command sa example na ito ang mga variable na iyon. Gamitin ang parehong Fortran compiler para sa mga binding at sa application, dahil espesipiko sa compiler ang mga module file. Ang pag-build ng Qiskit C library (`make c`) ay inaabot ng ilang minuto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
