msgid "The second command reads the `bitstrings_stepNN.txt` files written by the first, without submitting hardware jobs. Its `per-step` mode diagonalizes each file separately; it does not combine all files into one pooled subspace. `per-step` is the default with `--bitstrings-dir`, and `--mode pooled` is rejected there, because pooled mode runs the full circuit ensemble. Saved samples, including those from a hardware run, can therefore only be reprocessed per step.\n"
msgstr "Binabasa ng pangalawang command ang mga file na `bitstrings_stepNN.txt` na isinulat ng una, nang hindi nagsusumite ng mga hardware job. Dinidiagonalize ng `per-step` mode nito ang bawat file nang hiwalay; hindi nito pinagsasama ang lahat ng file sa iisang pooled subspace. Ang `per-step` ang default kapag may `--bitstrings-dir`, at tinatanggihan doon ang `--mode pooled`, dahil pinapatakbo ng pooled mode ang buong circuit ensemble. Kaya ang mga naka-save na sample, kasama ang mula sa hardware run, ay maaari lang iproseso muli kada step.\n"

