# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a backend available to your account with enough qubits for the model space; without `--backend`, the driver uses the least-busy backend. The driver transpiles each circuit, submits it as its own Sampler job, and waits for that job to finish before building the next circuit. The command shown therefore runs 11 jobs one after another, each with 4,096 shots on a 24-qubit register, and uses QPU time for each. If a job does not complete, the driver skips it and leaves its samples out of the pool. The driver also writes the returned samples to `bitstrings_stepNN.txt` files, which you can reprocess per step as shown in the previous section. Counts and energies depend on the samples and device noise.\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng backend na available sa account mo at may sapat na qubit para sa model space; kapag walang `--backend`, ginagamit ng driver ang least-busy na backend. Tina-transpile ng driver ang bawat circuit, isinusumite ito bilang sarili nitong Sampler job, at hinihintay na matapos ang job na iyon bago buuin ang susunod na circuit. Kaya ang ipinakitang command ay nagpapatakbo ng 11 job nang sunud-sunod, bawat isa ay may 4,096 shot sa 24-qubit register, at gumagamit ng QPU time sa bawat isa. Kung hindi nakumpleto ang isang job, nilalaktawan ito ng driver at hindi isinasama ang mga sample nito sa pool. Isinusulat din ng driver ang mga ibinalik na sample sa mga file na `bitstrings_stepNN.txt`, na maaari mong iproseso muli kada step gaya ng ipinakita sa nakaraang seksyon. Nakadepende ang mga bilang at energy sa mga sample at sa ingay ng device.\n"

