msgid "Both versions build the same shell-model Hamiltonian from the USDA interaction, which the regression test confirms for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$. They differ in how they choose the circuits and process the samples, so independently sampled runs are not expected to produce the same energy:\n"
msgstr "Binubuo ng dalawang bersyon ang parehong shell-model Hamiltonian mula sa USDA interaction, na kinukumpirma ng regression test para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$. Magkaiba sila sa kung paano nila pinipili ang mga circuit at pinoproseso ang mga sample, kaya hindi inaasahang magbibigay ng parehong energy ang mga takbong independiyenteng nag-sample:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | Fortran example | Python example |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Reference determinant | Fills the lowest single-particle-energy $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs of each species: $-28.644723$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ | Searches all paired fillings for the lowest diagonal energy: $-29.765549$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ |\n"
"| Circuit angles | Exact two-level mixing angle, $\\theta = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\operatorname{atan2}(2V, \\Delta)$ | First-order amplitude, $t = V/\\Delta$ |\n"
"| Samples with the wrong symmetry | Discarded by the symmetry filter | Repaired by self-consistent configuration recovery |\n"
"| Subspace | Unique kept determinants; whole shots are filtered on proton number, neutron number, $M_J$, and parity | Products of sampled proton and neutron half-configurations in the target $M_J$ and parity sector |\n"
"| Diagonalization | Pooled across all circuits, or per step | Pooled, inside the configuration-recovery loop |\n"
"| Backend | Named with `--backend`, otherwise the least-busy backend | `least_busy` backend with at least 40 qubits |\n"
"| Transpilation | Each circuit separately, optimization level 0 | All circuits together, optimization level 3 |\n"
"| Job submission | One job per circuit, one after another | One Sampler job per ensemble |\n"
"| Example run | 11 circuits × 4,096 shots for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ | 16 circuits × 10,000 shots each for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, and $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | Fortran example | Python example |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Reference determinant | Pinupuno ang mga $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pair na may pinakamababang single-particle-energy ng bawat species: $-28.644723$ MeV para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ | Hinahanap sa lahat ng paired filling ang pinakamababang diagonal energy: $-29.765549$ MeV para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ |\n"
"| Mga anggulo ng circuit | Eksaktong two-level mixing angle, $\\theta = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\operatorname{atan2}(2V, \\Delta)$ | First-order amplitude, $t = V/\\Delta$ |\n"
"| Mga sample na may maling symmetry | Itinatapon ng symmetry filter | Inaayos ng self-consistent configuration recovery |\n"
"| Subspace | Mga natatanging napanatiling determinant; sinasala ang buong shot ayon sa proton number, neutron number, $M_J$, at parity | Mga produkto ng na-sample na proton at neutron half-configuration sa target na $M_J$ at parity sector |\n"
"| Diagonalization | Pooled sa lahat ng circuit, o kada step | Pooled, sa loob ng configuration-recovery loop |\n"
"| Backend | Pinangalanan gamit ang `--backend`, kung hindi ay ang least-busy na backend | `least_busy` backend na may hindi bababa sa 40 qubit |\n"
"| Transpilation | Bawat circuit nang hiwalay, optimization level 0 | Lahat ng circuit nang sabay-sabay, optimization level 3 |\n"
"| Pagsusumite ng job | Isang job bawat circuit, sunud-sunod | Isang Sampler job bawat ensemble |\n"
"| Example run | 11 circuit × 4,096 shot para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ | 16 circuit × 10,000 shot bawat isa para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, at $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Appendix](#appendix) explains why the Python example searches for its reference determinant and uses the first-order amplitude. The Fortran application keeps the simpler choices, so its starting point is higher in energy for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, and its circuits seed different amplitudes. Because it discards rather than repairs samples with the wrong symmetry, low sample retention can also limit the accuracy of a Fortran result even though the Hamiltonian is correct.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag ng [Appendix](#appendix) kung bakit hinahanap ng Python example ang reference determinant nito at gumagamit ng first-order amplitude. Pinapanatili ng Fortran application ang mas simpleng mga pagpili, kaya mas mataas sa energy ang panimulang punto nito para sa $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, at ang mga circuit nito ay nag-seed ng ibang mga amplitude. Dahil itinatapon nito ang mga sample na may maling symmetry sa halip na ayusin, ang mababang sample retention ay maaari ring maglimita sa katumpakan ng resulta ng Fortran kahit tama ang Hamiltonian.\n"

